    "body": "## Context\nPR #119 has already merged the Stripe Connect recipient-onboarding foundation into `master`. This follow-up contains only the additional production hardening found during review.\n\n## Summary\n- request the Stripe `transfers` capability through the typed Java SDK contract\n- treat currently-due **and past-due** Stripe requirements as not payout-ready\n- serialize external recipient provisioning with a freshly locked user row, so stale principals or concurrent clicks cannot race the local mapping invariant\n- make future `stripe-connect` cash-out fail closed when onboarding is disabled\n- require a **fresh authoritative Stripe account refresh immediately before any future live wallet reservation**; cached readiness is never enough to reserve money\n- wire `PAYOUT_STRIPE_CONNECT_*` settings through Docker Compose so host configuration actually reaches the API container\n- extend Worker payout smoke to verify Flyway V44, disabled Connect behavior, and the unchanged sandbox ledger lifecycle\n- update payout documentation with the strengthened invariants\n\n## Financial / security invariants\n- this PR still registers **no live Stripe Connect payout dispatcher**; `PAYOUT_PROVIDER=stripe-connect` remains unavailable/fail-closed\n- sandbox `PAYOUT_RESERVE` / `PAYOUT_RESTORE`, idempotent request IDs, cancellation and settlement behavior are unchanged\n- no Stripe account ID or Account Link is exposed through public profile data\n- onboarding requires the latest locked user state to be ACTIVE and current doFast identity status to be VERIFIED\n- provider/account state is checked before future money reservation, not inferred from stale browser state\n- server-owned return/refresh URLs remain HTTPS-only outside localhost\n\n## Exact-head validation required\nHead: `215a3b29d58f6619e8b35a5d4d2f7f86e7f5604a`\n\n- Web verify: dependency audit + lint + production build\n- API verify: Maven verify\n- Containers/runtime smoke\n- Worker payout smoke\n\nDo not merge while any latest-head check is pending or failing. Any failure will be fixed on this same branch, followed by a full latest-head revalidation.",
